{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nThe `COMMITS` event and the `attach_commits` reducer already exist (`rebar.attach_commits`, `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py:697`, re-exported from `src/rebar/__init__.py`) and are used by the code-review workflow. Missing: an author-facing repair surface for a botched `rebar-ticket:` trailer, and a consumer. Approved design (b902-18af-14ed-4da1): expose retroactive commit linking on CLI + library + MCP, document it, then add a cheap deterministic close-gate check that linked commits' diffs match the recorded `file_impact`. OUT of scope: using linked commits as a completion-verifier diff basis (they may be incomplete, and CV already prefetches from `file_impact`).\n\n## Plan\n\n1. **Shared DET module** `src/rebar/_engine_support/commit_impact.py` (new, ~120 LOC): (a) `invalid_commit_shas(shas, repo_root)` via `git rev-parse --verify <sha>^{commit}`; (b) the step-4 path matchers, including `glob_match` — the repo's `**/`-aware semantics (`fnmatch(p,g) or (g.startswith(\"**/\") and fnmatch(p,g[3:]))`) from `src/rebar/llm/prompting/prompts.py:746`. Its ONLY true mirror is `src/rebar/llm/code_review/registry.py:242`; `src/rebar/grounding/oracle.py:316` uses PLAIN `fnmatch` with no `**/` handling, is NOT a copy, and is left untouched. The DET close path must not import `rebar.llm` (optional `[agents]` extra), so the helper is hoisted here and BOTH real copies (`prompts._glob_match`, `registry._glob_match`) become thin delegating wrappers — one implementation, no third copy.\n\n2. **CLI verb** `rebar attach-commits <ticket> <sha>...` wrapping the existing seam. Registration follows the established seam: add to `_WRITES_FULL` in `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py`; add a variadic handler (N SHAs) to `_ARGV_REGISTRY` in `src/rebar/_commands/__init__.py`; ship pinned help `src/rebar/_cli/help/attach-commits.txt` plus the `src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt` line (golden-pinned; `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py` requires it). Thin body in `src/rebar/_commands/attach_commits.py`.\n\n3. **Validation in the SEAM, not the CLI**, so all three surfaces inherit it identically: `rebar.attach_commits` calls `commit_impact.invalid_commit_shas` before appending. **ALL-OR-NOTHING** — the whole batch is validated first; if any SHA fails, NO `COMMITS` event is recorded and the call raises naming every offender. Union-add semantics unchanged. Library: `rebar.attach_commits` is already importable/re-exported — confirm and document. MCP: register `attach_commits` in `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py` with an `AttachCommitsResultOut` outputSchema model in `src/rebar/_mcp_models.py`, per the existing write-tool pattern (`mcp_server.py` only assembles registrars).\n\n4. **DET close check** in the existing completion precheck `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py` — the module that today raises \"cannot confirm the work landed\" (there is no `src/rebar/workflow/close_gate.py`). Commit discovery unions the two sources that already exist: (i) `state.commits` from COMMITS events; (ii) the precheck's own referencing-commit scan (`_referencing_commit_exists`, `close_precheck.py:94` — commits reachable from HEAD carrying a `rebar-ticket:` trailer or leading `<id>:` subject for the ticket or any transitive descendant). That function returns only a bool, so it is refactored into a SHA-returning `_referencing_commits(...)`, with `_referencing_commit_exists` kept as a thin wrapper — the documented monkeypatch target and its call sites keep working unchanged. For each commit, `git show --name-only` gives changed paths; a path neither covered by `file_impact` nor matched by this check's OWN exemption globs (`tests/**`, `docs/**`, `**/*.md`, `CHANGELOG.md` — owned here, not inherited) is a deterministic BLOCK naming the commit and paths. Matching (all via step 1, not re-derived): normalized repo-relative POSIX paths; a `file_impact` entry matches on exact equality, or as a directory prefix when it ends with `/` or names an existing directory; exemptions use `**/`-aware `glob_match`. No substring matching. No LLM.\n\n   **Git-error behavior, asymmetric by source:** a source-(ii) commit is present in this clone by construction, so a `git show` failure on it is anomalous and FAILS CLOSED (block, naming the SHA). A source-(i) SHA may legitimately be absent locally (attached from another clone, or unfetched), so it is SKIPPED, not blocked — blocking a foreign SHA would be a false positive on a repair surface whose purpose is recording commits.\n\n   A ticket with no discovered commits keeps today's behavior (the existing error); a ticket without `file_impact` is out of scope.\n\n5. **Remedy for a legitimate block:** the block message names the offending paths and says to declare them with `rebar set-file-impact <ticket> …`, after which close proceeds; the pre-existing `--force=\"<reason>\"` stays the break-glass.\n\n6. **Docs.** `docs/cli-reference.md` is GENERATED (`scripts/gen_cli_reference.py`, CI drift gate, subcommand count in header) so it is regenerated, not hand-edited. Hand-edited: `docs/mcp-reference.md` and `src/rebar/_guides/commit-ticket-trailer.md` (`rebar explain commit-trailer`). Each names the verb, when to use it, and the step-5 remedy.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `rebar attach-commits <ticket> <sha>` records a COMMITS event that `rebar show` reflects. Verify: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py -x`.\n- [ ] An invalid SHA is rejected with an error naming it. Verify: same file, test asserting the offending SHA appears in the error text.\n- [ ] A batch containing any invalid SHA records nothing (all-or-nothing). Verify: test asserting `state.commits` is byte-identical before/after a mixed valid/invalid batch.\n- [ ] The MCP server exposes `attach_commits` with an outputSchema, routed through the same seam. Verify: the MCP tool-inventory test asserts `\"attach_commits\"` is in the registered tool names.\n- [ ] A commit touching a path outside the declared `file_impact` blocks close, naming the offending path. Verify: unit test asserting the exact path string in the raised message.\n- [ ] A commit whose paths are all declared does not block close. Verify: unit test asserting close proceeds.\n- [ ] An exempt path does not block, including at the repo root (`README.md` under `**/*.md`). Verify: unit test over each exemption glob.\n- [ ] The DET check imports no `rebar.llm` module. Verify: test asserting `[m for m in sys.modules if m.startswith(\"rebar.llm\")] == []` after running it in a fresh interpreter.\n- [ ] The `**/`-aware glob semantics have one implementation. Verify: test asserting `prompts._glob_match` and `registry._glob_match` both delegate to `commit_impact.glob_match`.\n- [ ] An unreadable source-(ii) commit fails closed naming the SHA; an unresolvable source-(i) SHA is skipped without blocking. Verify: one unit test per direction.\n- [ ] `docs/mcp-reference.md` and `src/rebar/_guides/commit-ticket-trailer.md` name the verb and the `set-file-impact` remedy. Verify: `grep -E '^\\| `attach_commits`' docs/mcp-reference.md` and `grep -F 'rebar attach-commits' src/rebar/_guides/commit-ticket-trailer.md`.\n- [ ] `docs/cli-reference.md` is regenerated and its drift gate passes. Verify: `python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check` exits 0."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786514274517415001,"uuid":"1807fb9b-2bbb-4335-b308-f7ed5ac956b1"}